// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'fixture'. Valid alternatives: ['extends', '[', ':']
//
// A Mapping body is `(includeMapping)* (mappingElement)* (tests)? (testSuites)?`. Includes
// are a prefix, not a statement that may appear anywhere among the elements.
//
// The diagnostic is worth reading: by the time the parser reaches the misplaced `include`
// it has already left the include arm, so `include` is consumed as the head of a mapping
// ELEMENT (INCLUDE is one of the tokens `identifier` admits) and the complaint lands on the
// qualified name that follows. A rewrite that dispatches on the leading keyword never
// reaches that state and accepts the file.
###Mapping
Mapping fixture::neg::IncludeLate
(
   fixture::neg::Person: Relational
   {
      ~mainTable [fixture::neg::Db]T
      id: [fixture::neg::Db]T.ID
   }

   include fixture::neg::Base
)
